3. Functional Requirements:
3.1 System Features
Feature 1: User Authentication & Profile Management
Description: Allows customers and organizers to create accounts and authenticate securely.
Priority: High
Inputs: Name, Email, Password, Role (Buyer/Organizer).
Processing: Validate input format, hash password with bcrypt, issue JWT upon verification.
Outputs: Account creation confirmation or authorization token.
Feature 2: Interactive Seat Selection & Booking
Description: Displays venue seat map with real-time seat availability.
Priority: High
Inputs: Selected Event ID, Selected Seat Numbers (e.g., Row A, Seats 12-13).
Processing: Lock chosen seats temporarily (10-minute timer) to prevent double-booking.
Outputs: Seat reservation lock confirmation and total order calculation.
Feature 3: Payment Processing & Ticket Issuance
Description: Processes checkout total and generates a digital pass.
Priority: High
Inputs: Payment credentials, Promo code (optional).
Processing: Validate payment via external API, generate unique booking reference ID, attach encrypted QR code.
Outputs: Success screen with downloadable PDF/QR pass and confirmation email.
3.2 Use Case Specification
Use Case Name: Book Concert Ticket
Actors: Customer
Pre-conditions: User is logged in and event seats are unreserved.
Main Flow:
Customer searches and selects a concert.
Customer chooses available seats on the venue layout.
Customer clicks "Proceed to Payment" and inputs transaction credentials.
System confirms transaction, updates seat status to "Sold", and displays the QR ticket.
Alternate Flow: If payment fails, System releases seat lock and prompts user to retry.
Post-conditions: Ticket record stored in database with "Confirmed" status.

4. External Interface Requirements:
4.1 User Interfaces
Landing Page: Search bar, top trending concert banners, category navigation tags.
Seat Map UI: Visual grid with color-coded seats (Green = Available, Red = Sold, Yellow = Reserved).
Checkout Screen: Order summary, promo box, payment inputs.
4.2 Software Interfaces
Payment Gateway API: For transaction verification (e.g., Stripe API).
Email Service API: For automated QR-code ticket dispatch (e.g., SendGrid API).
4.3 Communication Interfaces
Protocol: HTTPS over TCP/IP.
Data Exchange Format: JSON.

5. Non-Functional Requirements:
5.1 Performance Requirements: Seat selection updates must render within 1.5 seconds; server must support up to 2,000 concurrent booking requests.
5.2 Security Requirements: Password encryption using bcrypt; role-based access control (RBAC); PCI-DSS compliance via payment gateways.
5.3 Reliability Requirements: 99.5% target system availability with database daily backup restoration capabilities.
5.4 Usability Requirements: Simple navigation layout requiring no more than 4 clicks to complete a booking.

6. Data Requirements
6.1 Data Description
User ID: Unique integer identifier for each customer or event organizer.
Event ID: Unique integer identifier for listed concerts or events.
Seat ID: Unique alphanumeric string representing seat placement (e.g., SEC-A-12).
Booking Reference: Unique encrypted string used for QR code generation.
Ticket Price: Decimal value representing cost per ticket.
Data Validation Rules: Email fields must conform to standard email regex patterns; ticket prices and seat counts must strictly be non-negative values.
6.2 Database Requirements
Users Table: Primary key (UserID), fields for Name, Email, PasswordHash, Role.
Events Table: Primary key (EventID), foreign key (OrganizerID), fields for Title, Category, Venue, Date, TotalSeats.
Seats Table: Primary key (SeatID), foreign key (EventID), fields for SeatNumber, Price, Status (Available, Locked, Sold).
Bookings Table: Primary key (BookingID), foreign keys (UserID, EventID), fields for TotalPrice, QRCodeURL, Timestamp.

7. Quality Attributes
Correctness: The system must accurately maintain seat inventory and ensure zero double-booking instances during high-volume sales.
Efficiency: High computational efficiency for processing rapid transaction locks (< 1.5 seconds) under concurrent user traffic.
Flexibility: Easy addition of new event types, promotional discount structures, or venue seating layouts without core architecture overhauls.
Reusability: Modular backend components (e.g., notification dispatcher, payment processor interface) designed to be reusable across future subsystem expansions.
Testability: High code coverage capability for automated unit and integration tests across payment gateways and booking logic.

8. Constraints and Risks
Constraints
Technical: System depends on HTTPS protocol standards and mandatory integration with certified third-party payment gateways.
Regulatory: Must comply with PCI-DSS guidelines for handling electronic payment data.
Risks
API Downtime: Failure or latency spike in external payment gateways (e.g., Stripe API) disrupting the checkout process.
Network Failures: Sudden dropped connections on mobile clients during seat lock or payment verification steps.
Security Threats: Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attacks or automated bot scraping during high-demand concert ticket launches.

9. Acceptance Criteria
Functional Verification: All primary user paths: user registration, event filtering, seat map rendering, seat locking, payment execution, and QR pass creation are completely verified without errors.
Concurrency Handling: The 10-minute seat locking mechanism successfully prevents double-booking scenarios when tested under simultaneous multi-user attempts for the same seat.
Payment Integration: 100% of mock transaction test cases (success, failure, timeout) return accurate system responses and status logs.
Performance Benchmarking: Page load time under 2 seconds and seat map response times under 1.5 seconds are verified.

9. Appendices & Glossary
Glossary
Buyer / Customer: End-user purchasing event tickets through the platform.
Event Organizer: Entity or user authorized to publish events, define seating charts, and set ticket prices.
Seat Lock: A temporary system lock (e.g., 10 minutes) placed on selected seats to prevent other users from booking them during checkout.
QR Code (Quick Response Code): A machine-readable 2D barcode containing encrypted booking validation data for gate access scanning.
PCI-DSS: Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard regulating secure handling of credit card information.
